CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "2c3c43fe-7cff-4324-ad4f-4318aae71ef6",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-22T01:33:10Z",
  "ticket_id": "fdeb-4c03",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "Phase 1 Step 2 probe table includes a seventh dimension 'Surface' asking where the feature manifests (web page, form, screen, CLI flag, endpoint, background job, internal API, migration, or 'no user-facing surface'); Understanding Summary renders a Surface bullet alongside Problem/Users/Scope/Success. Verified by: brainstorm progressive validation test asserts Surface is present in the Summary schema block of SKILL.md.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system properties (probe table dimension and Summary rendering) that will remain true after implementation, phrased as ongoing behaviors"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "UI intent detection runs on the confirmed Understanding Summary using a keyword first-pass (matching a project-configurable surface-lexicon, default shipped with the plugin, overridable via brainstorm.ui_keywords in dso-config.conf) and a haiku classifier on ambiguous matches. On classifier dispatch failure (Agent tool unavailable, MAX_AGENTS=0, timeout, malformed output), detection falls through to non-UI with a logged degradation notice. Verified by: regression test that seeds three cases (clear UI, clear non-UI, ambiguous with mocked classifier failure) and asserts UX probe set routing (fires / doesn't fire / falls back).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior and capability of how UI intent detection operates with specified fallback mechanisms"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When UI intent is detected and the ux_probe_fired flag for the current epic ID is unset, the static UX probe set runs once and sets the flag: three probes covering interaction criticality, non-happy-path state coverage, and flow entry/exit, asked as free-text follow-up questions in the Phase 1 dialogue. The flag is keyed by epic ID at $ARTIFACTS_DIR/ux-probe-fired-<epic-id> so sequential brainstorm runs for different epics cannot suppress each other's probes.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes the durable system behavior of how UX probes execute and flag state is managed across brainstorm runs"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Phase 1 Gate Step 2 (Intent Gap Analysis) and the UX probe checkpoint both loop back to Tell Me More whenever an intent gap surfaces that genuinely increases epic understanding. Termination requires that the gap analysis produces an empty gap list AND the user confirms the Understanding Summary in the same turn. No numeric cap.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior for how the workflow loops and terminates based on specific conditions, phrased as ongoing operational logic"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Brainstorm SKILL.md carries an explicit anti-redundancy directive: before forming any question, the agent must check (a) prior conversation turns semantically (recognising paraphrase and negative signals like 'I told you' / 'I answered that'), and (b) the codebase via Grep/Read/Glob. Duplicate questions prohibited. Verified by: regression test that seeds a user answer covering one of the three UX probe topics and asserts the corresponding probe is suppressed in the recorded question log.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (agent checks for redundancy before forming questions) that persists after implementation, verified by an ongoing regression test"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "For non-UI features, the UX probe set never fires; the non-UI cost is bounded to one keyword scan per confirmed Understanding Summary and zero classifier calls when the scan is unambiguous. Verified by: test run with a non-UI seed asserts the classifier dispatch code path is not entered (the degradation-notice log is the only emit path).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior and performance constraint that persists after implementation, verified by test assertions that check ongoing compliance"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "In non-interactive mode (BRAINSTORM_INTERACTIVE=false), the UX probe set is skipped entirely: emit INTERACTIVITY_DEFERRED with 'UX probes require user input' and tag the epic ui_probes:deferred so a subsequent interactive brainstorm run can complete them. Verified by: regression test invokes brainstorm with BRAINSTORM_INTERACTIVE=false on a UI seed and asserts (a) ui_probes:deferred tag is present on the resulting epic, (b) the probe questions are not asked.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where non-interactive mode consistently skips UX probes and defers them, verified by ongoing regression tests"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "End-to-end dogfooding validation (primary sprint-executable signal): a new test in tests/skills/brainstorm/ invokes the Phase 1 flow on a representative UI feature seed ('add a benefits-status dashboard for claimants'); stubs the haiku classifier to return 'ui'; asserts that (a) the Understanding Summary contains a Surface bullet, (b) all three UX probes are asked during Phase 1, (c) the resulting ticket description contains the UX probe answers in a structured location (inline in description or a ## UX Probes section). Test passes before epic closure. SCs 1-7 verify component-level contracts and are necessary but not sufficient for epic closure; SC8 is the authoritative integration signal.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time test creation and validation task that must be completed before epic closure, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
